  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Tennessee Jed** (1 review): Reviewer from Tennessee was delighted the band played Tennessee Jed [5]\n- **Scarlet Begonias** (1 other source): Scarlet Begonias segues directly into Fire on the Mountain [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Smokestack Lightening**: rare: 14 archived performances [7]\n- **Passenger**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 9 archived performances [7]\n- **Terripin Station**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Warf Rat**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Bobby Talks Politics**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **DeadCo61216Set2t04** (recommended): source not stated; 24 songs; 186 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Some phase shifting and scratching early, while the recorder was in a pocket, before it was fixed to a post; Small iPhone mics captured the bass well even though the taper stood far from the speaker stacks [5]\n- **deadandco2016-06-12**: audience recording; 16 songs; 182 min; rated 3.67/5 by 3 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Taper recorded from the edge of the handicapped bleacher at the What Stage, Bonnaroo, Manchester, TN [1]\n- Uploader links a Day Three Bonnaroo write-up covering Charles Bradley, Jason Isbell, Steep Canyon Rangers, Death Cab for Cutie and this set [2]\n- Reviewer says people near the taper chatted among themselves rather than paying attention to the band [3]\n- Reviewer calls it the best Dead and Company show so far [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **DeadCo61216Set2t04**: Audience recording made with an iPhone 6 Plus and a Tascam im2W mic strapped to a post, via a 30-pin adapter [1]\n- **deadandco2016-06-12**: taped by Phil Simon; transferred by Phil Simon; source: tascam DR 40 AUD [2]",
